course: dictionary
lesson: 10761
title: Use: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word use can be a verb or a noun. Most often it is a verb: to use something is to do something with it for a job or purpose. «Only an adult uses super glue» means an adult is the one who does the job with it, not a child. Uses, used and using are all forms of the same verb.
explain: When you use paint, food or money, some of it is gone. The battery sentence shows this: it pushes electricity round the circuit «until the chemicals are used up». Used up means all gone, so the chemicals are finished.
explain: Use can also mean the right or chance to use something. «The size of the hole decides which birds can use it» means which birds are allowed and able to use the nest box. A use is a purpose something can be used for, as in «a brick has many uses». Check the meaning by putting it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: Use is a verb (use, uses, used, using) and it can also be a noun: a use is a purpose.
fact: «Uses» is the form you need after he, she or it, as in «she uses a pencil».
fact: «Used up» means all gone: the chemicals in a battery are finished when they are used up.
fact: «It's no use» means it will not help, so it is not the same as useful.
fact: «British Sign Language (BSL) is a full language with its own grammar; it uses hand shapes, movements, the face and the body.»
exercise: «A battery pushes electricity round the circuit until the chemicals are used up.» What does used up mean here? | *All gone | Changed into light | Shared with a friend | Stored away for later
exercise: «Birds may nest in a nest box, and the size of the hole decides which birds can use it.» What does can use it mean? | Have to dig it | Must never go near it | *Are allowed and able to use it | Are too big to see it
exercise: «Only an adult uses super glue.» Find and copy the word that is a form of use. | *uses | only | adult | glue
test: «A punt is a flat-bottomed boat pushed along with a long pole; a painter is the rope at the front of a boat used to tie it up.» What does used mean here? | *Put to a purpose | Sold | Painted | Finished
test: «British Sign Language (BSL) is a full language; it uses hand shapes, movements, the face and the body.» Which word here is a verb? | BSL | movements | hand | *uses
exam: «Only an adult uses super glue.» What does uses mean here? | To hold tightly | To be finished | *To do something with it for a job or purpose | To feel tired
